@{
	ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="page-hero mb-4">
	<h1 class="mb-1">Privacy</h1>
	<p class="text-muted mb-0">Short version: no tracking, no ads, no analytics.</p>
</div>

<div class="card card-body shadow-sm">
	<h2 class="h5">Who runs this site</h2>
	<p>
		This is a personal, non-commercial website that shows my LEGO minifigure collection.
	</p>

	<h2 class="h5 mt-3">Visitors</h2>
	<p>
		You can browse the collection without an account. The site uses no analytics, no advertising
		and no tracking, and it loads nothing from other websites: fonts, scripts and images all come from this site.
	</p>

	<h2 class="h5 mt-3">Cookies</h2>
	<p class="mb-2">Only cookies the site needs to work are used:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Login cookie</strong>: only set when the site owner logs in to manage the collection.</li>
		<li><strong>Security cookie</strong>: protects forms (such as the login form) against forged submissions.</li>
		<li><strong>Message cookie</strong>: briefly stores a status message (for example "Saved") after an admin action.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Because these cookies are strictly necessary, no cookie consent banner is shown.</p>

	<h2 class="h5 mt-3">Stored in your browser</h2>
	<p>
		Your choice of light, dark or automatic theme is saved in your browser's local storage.
		It never leaves your device.
	</p>

	<h2 class="h5 mt-3">Server logs</h2>
	<p>
		Like most websites, the server keeps technical logs (such as IP address, time and requested page)
		to keep the site secure and to fix errors. Failed login attempts are logged together with
		the entered e-mail and IP address, to protect the admin account. Logs are kept only as long
		as needed for these purposes.
	</p>

</div>